<<<
He sces in England no attempt to mould history according to academic plans, but to direct it from case to case according to necessity (it is rather directed)./
===
*He sees in England* no attempt to *mould history according to academic plans,* but to *direct it from case to case according to necessity* (it is rather directed)./
>>>

<<<
There is no reason to suppose that the Government will accept any vital amendments, & most certainly not an amendment to eaclude Home Rule (& it will certainly not accept one)./
===
*There is* no reason to suppose *that the Government will accept any vital amendments,* & most certainly not *an amendment to exclude Home Rule* (& it will certainly not accept one)./
>>>

<<<
Although no party has been able to carry its own scheme out, it has been strong enough to prevent any other scheme being carried (each has been)./
===
*Although* no party *has been able to carry its own scheme out,* it *has been strong enough to prevent any other scheme being carried* (each has been)./
>>>

